## Schema Files (`defaults/schemas/`)

Schema file format, property types, and validation rules are documented in
[schema-system.mdc](mdc:.rulesdir/schema-system.mdc). The UI persists explicit
schema imports under `"imported_schemas"`; core validation merges persisted
schema definitions rather than widening one from JSONL records.

---

## Sample Data

`defaults/data/memory.jsonl` is the Foundation sample in canonical JSONL
format. The repository does not retain a legacy `.json` copy; use
`convert_memorymesh` for external legacy exports.

```bash
# Count nodes by type
jq -c 'select(.entitytype == "node") | .nodetype' defaults/data/memory.jsonl | sort | uniq -c

# Inspect a specific type
jq -c 'select(.entitytype == "node" and .nodetype == "npc")' defaults/data/memory.jsonl | head -2

# Find edges
jq -c 'select(.entitytype == "edge")' defaults/data/memory.jsonl | head
```
